flowchart TB
  accTitle: Five typed local repair operators
  accDescr: GraSP's local repair algebra uses five different operators. Rebind changes arguments for an existing skill. InsertPrereq adds missing prerequisite skills. Substitute replaces a skill with a compatible alternative. Rewire changes local dependencies, especially soft order edges. Bypass skips a node when the current state already satisfies its downstream requirements.
  F[Classified failure and affected subgraph] --> D{Diagnosis}
  D --> R[Rebind: change invocation arguments]
  D --> I[InsertPrereq: add prerequisite subgraph]
  D --> S[Substitute: replace skill schema]
  D --> W[Rewire: change local edges]
  D --> B[Bypass: skip already-satisfied work]
  R --> V[Validate proposed patch]
  I --> V
  S --> V
  W --> V
  B --> V
  V -->|Valid| X[Resume verified execution]
  V -->|Invalid or exhausted| E[Escalate to global replan or fallback]
  classDef source fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef process fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef output fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef caution fill:#FEF9E7,stroke:#F39C12,color:#1C1C1E
  class F source
  class D,V process
  class R,I,S,W,B output
  class X output
  class E caution
